# libafw headers

Documented in `include/afw_common.h`. Do not `#include "afw_common.h"` directly.

## Include hierarchy

```
afw_doxygen.h
  └─ afw_common.h (+ afw_common_opaques.h + generated afw_interface_opaques.h)
       └─ afw_interface.h              [GENERATED from generate/interfaces/afw_interface.xml]
            └─ afw_minimal.h           [cross-package-safe core subset]
                 └─ afw.h              [full public API — extensions / consumers]
                      └─ afw_internal.h [core libafw .c only — may change every build]
```

## Who includes what

| Context | Include |
|---------|---------|
| Core `src/afw/**/*.c` | **`afw_internal.h` only** (pulls `afw.h` + internals + generated registration) |
| Extension / command `.c` | **`afw.h`** — never `afw_internal.h` |
| New public module header | Prefer `#include "afw_interface.h"`; use `afw_minimal.h` only if it must stay in the minimal set (must not be pulled *by* `afw_minimal.h` itself) |
| Headers under `afw_minimal.h` | Only depend on `afw_interface.h` / non-AFW deps — keep the minimal contract |

## Hand vs generated headers

| Hand-edit | Never hand-edit |
|-----------|-----------------|
| `include/*.h` (umbrellas, common, minimal) | Entire `generated/` tree |
| `<module>/afw_*.h` and `*_internal.h` beside `.c` | `generated/afw_interface.h`, `afw_interface_opaques.h` |
| `generate/additional_includes/*.h` (injected into generators) | `afw_*_bindings.h`, `afw_data_type_*_binding.h`, `afw_strings.h`, `afw_const_objects.h`, `afw_declare_helpers.h`, `afw_generated.h`, `afw_version_info.h`, `afw_runtime_object_maps.h`, `*_impl_declares.h` |
| `generate/interfaces/*.xml`, `generate/objects/**`, `generate/strings/` | `generated/interface_closet/`, `function_closet/`, `ebnf/`, `objects/` copies, language bindings |

Top-level `generated/*.h` are installed/public (bindings, interface, strings). Closets and `generated/ebnf/` are **reference / docs only** — copy patterns into hand impls; do not ship logic only there.

## Generated header roles (quick)

- **`afw_interface.h`** — all interface structs/vtables/method typedefs (the C contract).
- **`afw_data_type_*` / `afw_function_bindings.h`** — create/evaluate/register surfaces for types and built-ins.
- **`afw_strings.h` / `afw_const_objects.h`** — permanent string/object instances.
- **`afw_generated.h`** — `afw_generated_register(xctx)` wires core metadata into the **environment** at create (see `afw-environment`).
- **`*_impl_declares.h`** — macros to declare an interface implementation (include from hand `.c`).

## Adding a public header

Drop `foo/afw_foo.h` under `src/afw` (outside `generate/`, `generated/`, `tests/`, `doc/`, `cmake/`). Next `./afwdev build --cdev -j` inventories it for install/include paths. If it is part of the public API, also add it to `include/afw.h`. If it is core-internal only, add it to `include/afw_internal.h` instead (name it `*_internal.h`).

**Install:** core `CMakeLists.txt` excludes `*_internal.h` and `afw_internal.h` from `PUBLIC_HEADER` install. CMake install is additive; `--cdev`/`--fulldev` both `--install`, then afwdev prunes leftover denylist names in the prefix include dir (not a wipe of sibling public headers). Monorepo **build** still sees full source includes. Settled model: `designs/libafw-headers-and-api-surface.md`.

**`.c` vs `.h`:** translation units use `afw.h` / `afw_internal.h`. Module headers use `afw_interface.h` or `afw_minimal.h` (bootstrap — not a thin app API). Do not put new core-only APIs on the `afw.h` list.

Related: `afw-core-layout`, `afw-generate-metadata`, `afw-c-runtime`.

## Doxygen comments in hand-written headers

Doxygen comments in `src/afw/**/*.h` (and `include/`) must be kept in sync with the declarations:

- `@param` names must **exactly** match the C parameter names (including case). No trailing dots or extra punctuation in the name.
- `@return` is only appropriate for non-`void` functions; remove inaccurate return documentation from `void` declarations.
- `@brief` and descriptive text should accurately reflect the function/macro being documented (avoid copy-pasted descriptions from similar functions).
- Comment blocks must be lexically balanced. Stray `*/` or unescaped `/*` sequences inside `/** ... */` blocks will trigger `-Werror=comment` during normal C compilation.
- Central rich group descriptions and mental models belong in `include/afw_doxygen.h` (`@defgroup`). Individual headers use `@addtogroup` + a `@file` block that says "See @ref ...".
- Prefer **`@addtogroup` of a canonical group** declared in `afw_doxygen.h` (or a deliberate nested `@defgroup` under it). Avoid inventing one-off group names per file that never appear in the tree.
- When editing a `/** @file … */` block, **preserve the long description** after `@brief` (blank ` *` line, then narrative / related headers / `@ref`). Only change that body when intentionally updating content—do not drop it in bulk cleanups.
- Interface **call macros** are the developer-facing API; their Doxygen comes from **interface XML + generators**, not from hand-editing `generated/`. See `afw-interfaces-doxygen`.

GitHub renders list markers (`-`, `*`, `+`) as bullets in the PR description view; the source uses dashes or asterisks.

After making Doxygen changes, run `./afwdev build --cdev -j` (and targeted tests) to ensure the comments do not break the build.
